      "worked": "Let $\\theta=\\angle ACB=\\angle DCE$ (vertically opposite angles).\n\nApply the sine rule in $\\triangle ABC$ and $\\triangle DEC$. Since $AC=CD$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{x}{\\sin\\theta}&=\\frac{AC}{\\sin30^\\circ}\\\\\n\\frac{y}{\\sin\\theta}&=\\frac{CD}{\\sin120^\\circ}\\\\\n\\frac{x}{y}&=\\frac{AC\\sin120^\\circ}{CD\\sin30^\\circ}\\\\\n\\frac{x}{y}&=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}/2}{1/2}=\\sqrt{3}\\\\\nx:y&=\\sqrt{3}:1.\n\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
